version: "0.6.0"

date-released: 2026-08-21

abstract: >
  CPC Validation is the reference validation framework for
  Constraint Physical Computing (CPC). It defines a canonical constraint IR,
  qualified RC, Digital, and FPGA execution backends, independent
  cross-backend semantic validation, and an RFC-0009 physical-evidence
  lifecycle. Version 0.6.0 adds the accepted RFC-0010 architecture for
  driven-dissipative open-system execution and referenced readout, together
  with an execution-specification model, conformance validation, and a
  simulated reference witness. The RFC-0009 P1 FPGA evidence remains the
  repository's concrete physical-execution milestone; RFC-0010 does not by
  itself establish a physical open-system realization.

